    {
      "id": "zvh3npc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Time Period of the Vedic Age"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vedic Age is broadly divided into the Early Vedic Period (1500–1000 BC) and Later Vedic Period (1000–600 BC).",
        "The four sacred Vedas are Rigveda (hymns), Samaveda (melodies), Yajurveda (sacrificial rituals), and Atharvaveda (charms and spells).",
        "Political organization evolved in hierarchical order: Kula (family) -> Grama (village) -> Vis (clan) -> Jana (people) -> Rashtra (territory).",
        "Popular assemblies like Sabha, Samiti, and Vidatha exercised legislative and judicial control over the Rajan (King).",
        "The economy shifted from pastoralism in the Rigvedic era to settled agriculture aided by iron technology (Shyama Ayas) in the Later Vedic era."
      ],
      "id": "w2wtfli"
    },
