      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nw0fty7",
      "content": "• Rigveda is the oldest Veda"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Indra (Purandhara - destroyer of forts) is the most praised deity in Rigveda with 250 dedicated hymns.",
        "Atharvaveda explicitly mentions Sabha and Samiti as the two daughters of Prajapati.",
        "The Battle of Ten Kings (Dasrajan War) was fought on the banks of the Parushni (Ravi) river.",
        "Iron was referred to as 'Shyama Ayas' or 'Krishna Ayas' during the Later Vedic Period."
      ],
      "id": "x54ehqg"
    },
